{"id":"h290","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Magna Carta was sealed in 1215.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"King John sealed Magna Carta at Runnymede on 15 June 1215 after negotiations with rebel barons.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The charter's own text and contemporary chronicles such as Coggeshall and Wendover record the 1215 date.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The charter is widely cited by the year 1215.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The charter was not a single fixed document at the moment of sealing.","confidence":0.5,"lean":-1,"theta":0.7854,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Later reissues in 1216, 1217 and 1225 revised and reduced the clauses.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Pope Innocent III annulled the 1215 charter soon after, and the war between John and the barons continued.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":1.443},{"text":"The reissues and annulment do not change that the sealing occurred in 1215, so they do not contradict the claim.","confidence":0.93,"lean":1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The claim concerns only the year of sealing, and multiple primary and secondary sources agree on 1215.","confidence":0.93,"lean":1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The claim that the Magna Carta was sealed in 1215 is true.","confidence":0.96,"lean":1,"theta":1.508,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.8,